.TH SEMVER-FORGE 1 "2026-10-25" "semver-forge 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
semver-forge \- semantic version calculation and local Git release management
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B semver-forge
.RI [ global-options ]
.I command
.RI [ command-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B semver-forge
calculates Semantic Versioning 2.0.0 versions from Conventional Commit history, synchronizes configured version metadata, generates release notes, and creates local Git release tags.
.PP
Package building, testing, artifact collection, and publishing are separate project or CI responsibilities. SemVer Forge does not perform them.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --help ,\ -h
Show command help.
.TP
.B --version
Print the installed program version.
.TP
.BI --project \ DIR
Use the specified project directory.
.TP
.B --json
Emit JSON output where supported.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Discover project metadata and version files, report conflicting version values, and create one SemVer Forge configuration. Existing configuration files are reused; duplicate SemVer Forge TOML files are an error.
.TP
.B doctor
Inspect Git, Python, repository state, configuration, and version-source health.
.TP
.B current
Display the canonical version and its source.
.TP
.B validate VERSION
Validate a SemVer version string.
.TP
.B compare VERSION_A VERSION_B
Compare versions by SemVer precedence.
.TP
.B bump patch|minor|major
Calculate an increment; synchronize files only with --write.
.TP
.B next [--explain]
Calculate the next version from commits since the latest recognized release boundary.
.TP
.B sync [--version VERSION] [--dry-run]
Synchronize the canonical version and configured targets.
.TP
.B changelog [--dry-run]
Generate release notes from commits in the proposed release range and insert a version section into the configured changelog file. With --dry-run, print the complete proposed changelog without writing it. An existing section for the proposed version is an error.
.TP
.B release [patch|minor|major] [options]
Update configured version files and changelog, optionally commit those changes, and create a local Git tag. Options include --version VERSION, --prerelease alpha|beta|rc, --dry-run, --notes-only, and --yes. There is no --build option.
.TP
.B check
Check agreement between the canonical version and synchronization targets.
.TP
.B status
Summarize working-tree state, current version, latest release tag, and proposed next version.
.TP
.B history
Show commits since the release boundary.
.TP
.B verify-tag
Verify the latest recognized release tag.
.TP
.B verify-release
Verify the latest release tag and whether it points to HEAD.
.TP
.B install [--prefix DIR]
Install the source-tree package into a prefix.
.TP
.B uninstall [--prefix DIR]
Remove recognized installation files under a prefix.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .semver-forge.toml
Preferred project configuration file.
.TP
.I semver-forge.toml
Supported legacy configuration filename. Do not keep both names.
.TP
.I VERSION
Common canonical version source.
.TP
.I CHANGELOG.md
Optional generated changelog.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
semver-forge init
semver-forge doctor --json
semver-forge next --explain
semver-forge release --dry-run
semver-forge release patch --yes
semver-forge verify-release
.fi
.SH SAFETY
Release execution requires a clean working tree by default. Existing tags are never moved or overwritten. SemVer Forge does not build, test, publish, or push release artifacts.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Git is the implemented VCS backend. Version synchronization is limited to the adapters documented in docs/CONFIGURATION.md.
